{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:44:03Z","thinking":"**Refining Search Query Matching**\n\nThe current implementation in the route file struggles with exact matches because of spaces or slight variations in the input query. The regex search, specifically `/napa 500mg/i` for \"Napa 500 mg\", will fail. A more robust solution requires improving how the query tokens are cleaned.\n\n\n**Improving Search with Tokenization**\n\nThe system attempts an exact match using regex with the raw query first. If that fails, it cleans the query by removing non-alphanumeric characters and splitting into tokens. It then strips units like \"mg\" from tokens and constructs regex for both exact and partial token matches across multiple fields.\n\nThe initial token search tries to match all tokens, then broadens the search to find any of the tokens in the name or generic name, which accounts for slight variations like \"Napa 500 mg\" vs \"napa 500\".\n\n\n**Improving Search Failure Handling**\n\nIf an exact or tokenized match fails, the system should offer suggestions. It will fetch a limited set of medicine names to present alternatives to the user. These suggestions will appear as options if an exact match is not found.\n\nThe system will display a message, along with the suggestions, and will also offer the options to register a new medicine or to report an unregistered medicine. This will enable users to easily contribute to and complete the database.\n\nIf a medicine is found, but isn't stocked by any pharmacy, reference pricing can be presented. This is based on benchmarks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\server\\\\seed\\\\seedData.js\"","EndLine":"400","StartLine":"360","toolAction":"\"View end of medicinesData in seedData.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Check medicinesData array end\""}}]}
